# More machines for scripts/test-linux.sh, which needs none: it always runs
# the real-kernel checks on this machine (in a container when this is not
# Linux). Each machine listed here runs them too, over SSH, and the script
# fails if one of them cannot be reached.
#
# One machine per line: <rust-target> <ssh-destination>
#
#   aarch64-unknown-linux-musl user@arm-host
#   x86_64-unknown-linux-musl  user@x86-host
#
# For a single run, give the same pairs to the script instead:
#
#   scripts/test-linux.sh aarch64-unknown-linux-musl user@arm-host
